        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f9ed97c3-7b40-50ac-9466-1b8673ac8359",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Interact Model One Home Computer, Sord M5, CGL M5, Game M5\n- Companies: Protecto Enterprizes, Computer Games Limited, Takara, Highland Appliance, Newman Computer Exchange\n- Places: Barrington, Illinois, Chicago, Detroit, Ann Arbor, Japan, United Kingdom, Czechoslovakia, South Korea\n- Events: Consumer Electronics Show\n- Topics: mail order sales, home computer markets, exports\n\nFacts:\n- The Interact Model One Home Computer debuted at the Consumer Electronics Show in Chicago in June 1978 at a price of $499.\n- Most Interact Model One Home Computers were sold by the liquidator Protecto Enterprizes of Barrington, Illinois through mail order sales.\n- Interact Model One Home Computers were also sold through mail order houses and at Highland Appliance in the Detroit, Michigan area and Newman Computer Exchange in Ann Arbor.\n- The Sord M5 primarily competed in the Japanese home computer market.\n- The Sord M5 was sold in the United Kingdom as the CGL M5 by Computer Games Limited.\n- The Sord M5 was reasonably popular in Czechoslovakia, where it was one of the first affordable computers available to the general public.\n- Takara sold Sord M5 models in Japan as the Game M5, and Sord M5 models were also exported to South Korea.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2080c132-878a-51c3-aa91-51a85aede925",
        "text": "Page: Interact Home Computer. Sentence: Most were sold by the liquidator \"Protecto Enterprizes\" of Barrington, Illinois through mail order sales.\nPage: Interact Home Computer. Sentence: The Interact Model One Home Computer debuted at the Consumer Electronics Show in Chicago in June 1978 at a price of $499.\nPage: Interact Home Computer. Sentence: The majority of sales were thru Mail Order houses and you could buy it off the shelf at Highland Appliance in the Detroit, MI area and Newman Computer Exchange in Ann Arbor.\nPage: Sord M5. Sentence: Primarily the Sord M5 competed in the Japanese home computer market.\nPage: Sord M5. Sentence: It was also sold as the CGL M5 in the United Kingdom by Computer Games Limited, and was reasonably popular in Czechoslovakia, where the M5 stood as one of the first affordable computers available to the general public.\nPage: Sord M5. Sentence: Takara also sold models in Japan as the Game M5, and models were also exported to South Korea.",
